<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Paranagua/Santos sugar shipping conditions.</title>
<headline>Brazil Paranagua/Santos sugar shipping conditions.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Brazilian ports of</p>
<p>Paranagua and Santos reported the following conditions for</p>
<p>shipping sugar.</p>
<p>PARANAGUA:</p>
<p>Vessels: Nika loading 14,000 tonnes bagged sugar. Christos M loading 25,000 tonnes bulk sugar. Waiting to dock, six vessels to load bagged sugar and two to load bulk.</p>
<p>Road: no figures available.</p>
<p>Loading (July 25-27): 9,210 tonnes using big bags and 36,227</p>
<p>tonnes bulk.</p>
<p>Stocks: no figures available.</p>
<p>SANTOS:</p>
<p>Vessels: Icarus, Seanav I, Libanus and George B. each loading</p>
<p>14,000 tonnes bagged sugar. Mattz Spica loading 12,000 tonnes</p>
<p>bagged sugar. Nordpol loading 41,000 tonnes bulk sugar. Delta</p>
<p>Freedom loading 13,125 tonnes sugar. Valentin Khutorsk loading</p>
<p>12,500 tonnes bagged sugar. Waiting to dock, three vessels to</p>
<p>load bulk sugar and three to load sugar (unspecified). At Cargill private terminal, Rhea loading 25,000 tonnes bulk sugar. Waiting to dock, two vessels to load sugar</p>
<p>(unspecified).</p>
<p>Stocks: 9,535 tonnes bulk in CODESP warehouses, no bagged sugar. Private warehouses already with bagged sugar but stock levels unavailable.</p>
<p>((--Joelle Diderich, Sao Paulo newsroom +55 11 248 5417))</p>
</text>
